{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786928034170920001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"amoebaean-hemihedral-vervet","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"0a5cd06680cf298e95cc8a232783a888e7772c663374150786bdd39f53c6a7d0","event_uuid":"b0b626b1-5e5c-4658-b27b-43ac1e4c41ac","position":{"commit_sha":"9ae657c2f4ebe684aae3ccd62daae0bcfcef740d","position":"1786924755313354001-b0b626b1-5e5c-4658-b27b-43ac1e4c41ac"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8839c4e7b91e96abff98321e229b471fce0e577deae386c5d18804680a0eede9","event_uuid":"1d42f1f2-ad3e-4dc3-bb20-16b4e4d7e6cf","position":{"commit_sha":"4ae32da6479f0b6ba68186b5e4a66df4622021b8","position":"1786924824966602001-1d42f1f2-ad3e-4dc3-bb20-16b4e4d7e6cf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9eaf877db8b4a8d8c0552f4c0ae6b9f5484ff6d70ca9cb7c885d782dcdab137d","event_uuid":"b55b78ef-b367-48e5-85ad-cf89ee973977","position":{"commit_sha":"9f3441c27db06ee34da2db0364fe30fb509bf702","position":"1786924852082784001-b55b78ef-b367-48e5-85ad-cf89ee973977"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786924755313354001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b55b78ef-b367-48e5-85ad-cf89ee973977","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"66b3-4214-c70b-4a9a"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nPydantic deliberately counts one Agent-visible model turn even when `FallbackModel` tries multiple candidates inside it. The approved RP-01 decision follows maintained-project practice: keep that request budget authoritative and make candidate activity operationally visible as tracing, not as `candidate_requests` in usage. Current candidate construction is centralized in `model_classes.build_fallback_model` and `runner.PydanticAIRunner` already records ordered candidate provenance (`src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py:414+`, `src/rebar/llm/runner.py:372-465`).\n\n## Approach\nInstrument each already-built fallback or native-to-prompted candidate at the public Pydantic model boundary, preserving the Agent model-request span as the logical-turn parent. Candidate child spans record stable order, provider-qualified model identity, returned or raised outcome, and provider-reported usage when available. Use the existing optional tracing setup, so the base installation stays import-clean and a missing tracing exporter is a no-op. Do not alter `FallbackModel` selection, `ProviderSession` lifecycle, `RunUsage`, `UsageLimits`, pricing, or JSONL. Provider SDK/HTTP retries remain outside this candidate layer and are never inferred.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py` — wrap the concrete candidate models at construction without changing order or fallback predicates.\n- `src/rebar/llm/tracing.py` — define bounded candidate span attributes through the existing optional tracing seam.\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — pass candidate order/provenance into instrumentation without adding retry policy.\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py`, `tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py` — candidate order, outcome, provenance, and usage non-interference.\n- New focused tracing test module using an in-memory exporter from the existing tracing development dependency.\n\n## Testing\n- Primary 503 then fallback success yields one Agent request and two ordered candidate spans.\n- All candidates fail yields two error spans and the existing ordered `FallbackExceptionGroup`.\n- Native-schema rejection then prompted success yields two candidate spans and one Agent request.\n- Tracing disabled yields identical result, usage, imports, and exception behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Primary-failure/fallback-success emits two ordered candidate spans beneath one logical Agent request span, with the fallback model recorded as the answer; verified by an in-memory exporter test.\n- [ ] All-candidate failure emits one sanitized error outcome per attempted candidate and preserves the existing ordered exception group and resolution classification; verified by fallback-chain tests.\n- [ ] Native-to-prompted downgrade emits native-raised then prompted-returned candidate outcomes without adding an Agent request or changing fallback eligibility; verified by a focused downgrade trace test.\n- [ ] Candidate spans contain no prompt, response, credential, endpoint secret, or unsanitized exception body when content tracing is disabled; verified by secret-canary assertions.\n- [ ] `_usage`, `UsageLimits`, pricing, and durable usage JSONL are identical with tracing on and off and contain no candidate counter; verified by paired-result assertions.\n- [ ] Importing and running the base installation without the tracing extra remains successful and creates no span dependency error; verified by the lean-import subprocess test.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py","reason":"instrument concrete fallback candidates without changing selection"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/tracing.py","reason":"add bounded candidate span attributes"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner.py","reason":"thread candidate order and provenance into instrumentation"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py","reason":"pin candidate trace order and fallback behavior"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py","reason":"pin provenance and usage non-interference"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_candidate_tracing.py","reason":"add in-memory span and lean-import contracts"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","66b3-4214-c70b-4a9a"],["parent","905d-1287-effc-4a83"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"905d-1287-effc-4a83","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["janitor","rp01","llm","tracing"],"ticket_id":"2e1b-6517-eb1e-4309","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-01 S4 — Trace fallback and downgrade candidates without redefining usage","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b0b626b1-5e5c-4658-b27b-43ac1e4c41ac","1d42f1f2-ad3e-4dc3-bb20-16b4e4d7e6cf","b55b78ef-b367-48e5-85ad-cf89ee973977"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786928034170920001,"uuid":"d831d8f1-5906-4c8e-bf82-38acbd5729b5"}